  "guideCodex3": "In the Codex IDE extension, open the gear menu, select MCP servers, then Restart extension. In the CLI, start a new session: /mcp lists antenna.",
  "guideClaudeDesktop1": "Open Claude Desktop. In the menu bar choose Claude → Settings…, open the Developer tab and select Edit Config: it shows claude_desktop_config.json.",
  "guideClaudeDesktop2": "Add this entry under \"mcpServers\", keeping the other servers:",
  "guideClaudeDesktop3": "Quit Claude Desktop completely and open it again.",
  "guideClaudeDesktop4": "Check: in a chat, open “Add files, connectors, and more”, then Connectors → Manage connectors: Antenna is listed.",
  "guideClaudeCode1": "In the Terminal, add Antenna to Claude Code for your user:",
  "guideClaudeCode2": "Start claude: /mcp shows antenna. Claude Code starts MCP servers after you answer whether you trust the folder.",
  "guideClaudeCode3": "Simpler: “Start in Code mode” runs Claude Code in Antenna's window with Antenna connected and Antenna's check before every tool, with nothing to type.",
  "guideGemini1": "In the Terminal, add Antenna to Gemini CLI for your user (without -s user it goes into this folder's project settings):",
  "guideGemini3": "In Gemini CLI, run /mcp reload (or start it again): /mcp lists antenna.",
  "guideCursor1": "“Connect” opens Cursor's install link: Cursor shows Antenna and asks you to install it.",
  "guideCursor3": "Restart Cursor after editing the file. Cursor lists MCP under its paid plan.",
  "guideVscode1": "“Connect” opens VS Code's install link: VS Code shows Antenna and asks you to install it.",
  "guideVscode2": "Or open the Command Palette, run “MCP: Open User Configuration” and add this under \"servers\":",
  "guideVscode3": "Or add it from the Terminal:",
  "guideVscode4": "VS Code asks you to trust the server when it first starts. With Copilot Business or Enterprise, your organization's “MCP servers in Copilot” policy must be on.",
  "guideDevin2": "Or add it from the Terminal (-s user makes it apply everywhere):",
  "guideDevin3": "Restart Devin Desktop. Windsurf is now Devin Desktop; its MCP settings moved to this file.",
  "guideZed1": "In Zed, open Settings → AI → MCP Servers (or the “agent: open settings” action), click Add Server, then choose Add Local Server.",
  "guideZed2": "Give the name, the command and its arguments. In Zed's settings file the entry looks like this:",
  "guideZed3": "Zed uses the server's tools and prompts.",
  "guideLmStudio1": "“Connect” opens LM Studio's install link (Add to LM Studio); confirm it there.",
  "guideLmStudio2": "Or open the Program tab, then Install → Edit mcp.json, and add this entry. LM Studio loads it when you save.",
  "guideGrok1": "In the Terminal, add Antenna to Grok Build:",
  "guideGrok3": "In Grok, type /mcps (press r to refresh), or run grok mcp doctor.",
